What does this JavaScript print? Type the number.

```js
const ia = new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4));
ia[0] = 5;
console.log(Atomics.compareExchange(ia, 0, 5, 9));
```

What does this print in Node.js?

```js
const ia = new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4));
ia[0] = 9;
const r = Atomics.compareExchange(ia, 0, 5, 7);
console.log(r, ia[0]);
```

Several threads double a shared value with this loop. What happens when another thread changes `counter` between the `get()` and the first CAS?

```java
int cur = counter.get();
while (!counter.compareAndSet(cur, cur * 2)) {
  // retry
}
```

A producer publishes a node to a consumer like this. What can go wrong?

```cpp
// producer
node->value = 42;
head.store(node, std::memory_order_relaxed);

// consumer
Node* n = head.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
if (n) use(n->value);
```

This C++ code tries a single compare-exchange to claim a slot and reports "taken" on failure. What is the bug?

```cpp
int expected = 0;
if (!slot.compare_exchange_weak(expected, myId)) {
  return Status::Taken;
}
return Status::Claimed;
```

A developer "fixes" a stale-value bug in a Java CAS loop like this. Does it now update `balance` correctly under concurrency?

```java
long cur = balance.get();
long next = applyFee(cur);
while (!balance.compareAndSet(balance.get(), next)) {
  // retry
}
```
